$ whycant -u root exec /home/alice/tool.sh

✗ root (uid 0) cannot exec /home/alice/tool.sh

  /                     drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /home                 drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /home/alice           drwxr-xr-x  alice:alice  ✓ traverse
  /home/alice/tool.sh   -rw-r--r--  alice:alice  ✗ exec   ← blocked here

Why
  root bypasses most permission checks, but the kernel only runs a file
  if at least one execute bit is set, and /home/alice/tool.sh has mode -rw-r--r--.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Make the file executable for its owner:
       chmod u+x /home/alice/tool.sh
